+
+## 14. Conversation list (#144)
+
+### Client request: `list_conversations`
+
+| Field              | Type    | Required      | Description                                   |
+| ------------------ | ------- | ------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`             | string  | Yes           | `"list_conversations"`                        |
+| `limit`            | integer | No            | 1–200                                         |
+| `before`           | object  | No            | Composite cursor containing both fields below |
+| `before.updatedAt` | string  | With `before` | Date string accepted by `Date.parse`          |
+| `before.sessionId` | string  | With `before` | Session id breaking ties on activity          |
+
+Validation is independent of configuration and names an invalid window field; undeclared fields, including `userId`, are discarded ([validated by: validates history windows independently of deployment settings](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L117)).
+
+### Server response: `conversation_list`
+
+| Field                        | Type                  | Description                                           |
+| ---------------------------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`                       | string                | `"conversation_list"`                                 |
+| `conversations`              | ConversationSummary[] | Newest activity first, session id descending for ties |
+| `conversations[].sessionId`  | string                | Id usable with the existing resume query              |
+| `conversations[].createdAt`  | string                | ISO creation time                                     |
+| `conversations[].updatedAt`  | string                | ISO activity time                                     |
+| `conversations[].entryCount` | number                | Number of stored entries                              |
+
+**GDPR.** This response carries only one authenticated user's own conversation metadata and no conversation content or credentials, takes the user id from the connection rather than the frame, and is sent only when asked with `transport.history.enabled`; enabling history is the deployer's decision to make that metadata reachable from a client ([validated by: lists only the authenticated user metadata and pages into the existing resume path](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L171)).
+
+The request runs outside the turn lock and introduces no `stream_end` ([validated by: answers history before the active turn releases its session lock](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L211)).
+
+Disabled or unavailable history answers `UNSUPPORTED`, while an operational store failure answers a sanitized `SERVER_ERROR` and leaves the socket open, never disguising failure as an empty history ([validated by: refuses unavailable history and sanitizes store failures without closing the socket](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L244)).
